IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-vintages`

-- int-vintage.l4: how a headline function of the integration layer is asked about a DAY when the text of the Law changed during that day.
-- Group G7's resolver refuses a question about the day alone on 27 February 2024 (the text changed at 9.30 a.m.: R&O.10/2024; fork F7.1, reading taken).
-- A headline whose answer does not depend on which of the two texts applies would refuse for no reason, so the integration layer asks the question under EACH text in force at some time on the day
-- (group G7's `Endnotes: the texts in force at some time on`) and answers only if the answers agree; otherwise it refuses with a reason that says so. (Assumed, not ruled: see NOTES.md, the consistency register.)
-- A question about a day with exactly one text is asked under that text; a day before the first consolidated text is asked under `before the first consolidated version`, which the groups' rules refuse.

§ `Integration layer -- the text of the Law on a day`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Int refusal: the text of the Law changed during the day and the two texts answer differently` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 changed during the day asked (R&O.10/2024 took effect at 9.30 a.m. on 27 February 2024) and the two texts give different answers: ask by instant, or accept the answer of one text"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Int refusal: no text of the Law is in force on the day` MEANS
    REFUSE "no text of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 is in force on the day asked"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      day IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The readings of group G7 (fork F7.1 decides whether a day on which the text changed is refused or counted wholly in the new text)
      question IS A FUNCTION FROM `Vintage of the text` TO a @desc The question, asked of one text of the Law
GIVETH AN a
`Int the answer under every text of the Law in force on` day interp question MEANS
    CONSIDER `Endnotes: the texts in force at some time on` day interp
      WHEN EMPTY THEN `Int refusal: no text of the Law is in force on the day`
      WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF all (GIVEN other YIELD question other EQUALS question first) rest
        THEN question first
        ELSE `Int refusal: the text of the Law changed during the day and the two texts answer differently`
